<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<vmConfigs>
<!--
  Virtual machine configuration properties to collect (VCF Content Factory
  vCommunity).

  Name vSphere API properties of a virtual machine, as dotted paths, whose
  value you want on each virtual machine. A path is one or more names
  separated by dots; each name starts with a letter and holds only letters and
  digits (no spaces, brackets, slashes or trailing dot). A path that is not
  written this way is skipped and reported before anything is read. A path
  that vCenter does not know is dropped and reported, and costs no other value.
  Only values that are a single text, number, flag or choice are published;
  a path that leads to a whole object or a list is skipped and reported.

  Format
    - Separate entries with commas. A line break does NOT separate entries.
    - An XML comment, like this one, is ignored. To switch an entry on, move
      it out of the comment, and keep the comma after it.
    - Do not write two hyphens in a row inside a comment.

  Do not edit this shipped file: every upgrade of the pack replaces it and
  your edits are lost (measured on VCF Operations 9.0.2 and 9.1.1, even without force
  content update). Back the files up before an upgrade. Make a copy under another name in the VCF Operations configuration-file store, and
  enter that name (no .xml) in the account's VM Options Config File field. As shipped,
  every entry is commented out, so nothing is collected.

  Examples, one per line:
    config.firmware,
    config.cpuHotAddEnabled,
    config.memoryHotAddEnabled,
    config.changeTrackingEnabled,
    config.hardware.numCoresPerSocket,
-->
</vmConfigs>
